From 6c7685300ceedd0903a3c0025f53e44791af3c5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oaradla <339301037+Oaradla@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:31:38 +0000
Subject: SD bootloader: boot state file with trial start and rollback

ngCfg.json "general.stateFile" names a small state file on the card
(32 bytes, magic NGS1, CRC-32). A slot marked pending is started once
as a trial; an unconfirmed start, a failed load or a watchdog reset
falls back to the active slot and records the result, so a firmware
update cannot leave the box without a working image. A trial counts
only right before the jump, and a pending image that cannot be read
falls back in the same start. A slot picked by hand with the ears
starts normally and leaves the pending trial as it is. The file is
rewritten in place through a direct sector write, FatFs stays
read-only. Before the jump the bootloader leaves a handover record at
0x20003FE0 for SD images that are not the original firmware; both
linker scripts check that the bootloader's data stays below it. An SD
image that would not fit below the bootloader or is shorter than its
hash is not loaded.

The SD card stays powered when an SD image is started: a short supply
off phase left the card busy in ACMD41.

An empty battery broke down under the start load and restarted the box
in a loop: the battery is checked before the peripheral supply comes on
and again 20 ms after peripherals and SD card are on (the level is
logged in the debug build; both checks use the built-in minimum level,
as ngCfg.json is not read yet), and the network processor is started
only for a slot that needs the bootinfo or a flash image, which is
checked only when its slot is started. When the custom firmware's
retained record shows that the last start broke down in its network
processor start and no charger is connected, a pending trial is given
back without counting the try: the box blinks five times slowly and
hibernates until an ear or the charger wakes it. The low battery check
itself blinks and hibernates as before. The preloader in the flash is
unchanged.
